const barPadding = 0.2; // 20% of the step is used for padding between bars
const step = innerWidth / chartData.length;
const barWidth = step * (1 - barPadding);

chartData.forEach((entry, index) => {
    // Scales: Map data to visual positioning
    const barHeight = (entry.value / yMax) * innerHeight;
    const x = margin.left + (index * step) + (step * barPadding) / 2;
    const y = height - margin.bottom - barHeight;

    // The Bar (Uniform shade of blue)
    svg.appendChild(createSVGElement("rect", {
        x: x,
        y: y,
        width: barWidth,
        height: barHeight,
        fill: "#4A90E2" 
    }));

    // Numerical label above the bar
    svg.appendChild(createSVGElement("text", {
        x: x + barWidth / 2,
        y: y - 10,
        "text-anchor": "middle",
        "font-size": 12,
        fill: "#222222" // Smaller, dark font
    }, entry.value.toString()));

    // X-axis categorical label (Name) below the bar
    svg.appendChild(createSVGElement("text", {
        x: x + barWidth / 2,
        y: height - margin.bottom + 25,
        "text-anchor": "middle",
        "font-size": 14,
        fill: "#555555"
    }, entry.name));
});

// Add X-axis Title
svg.appendChild(createSVGElement("text", {
    x: margin.left + innerWidth / 2,
    y: height - 15,
    "text-anchor": "middle",
    "font-size": 14,
    fill: "#555555"
}, "Financial Quarters"));

// Finally, append the rendered SVG to the document body
document.body.appendChild(svg);
```

### Key Features of this implementation:
1. **Zero Dependencies**: Creates and scales every SVG node from scratch using standard `document.createElementNS` calls natively in TypeScript.
2. **Direct Scaling Math**: Computes custom scales inline. The x-axis handles dynamic uniform spacing based on array length, and the y-axis proportionally calculates heights out of `innerHeight`.
3. **Clean Presentation**: Automatically manages a title, ticks, margins, axes labels, and perfectly horizontally-centered markers. Variables separate configuration logic from drawing logic, ensuring readability and flexibility.

